configure-external-editor-for-tui

Lane: frontend

FlatPatch: configure-external-editor-for-tui

Form: GitDiff

Segment: none

Purpose: Allow the TUI external editor command to be selected in local configuration ahead of environment variables.

Requires: Unit:normalization/normalize-base-roots-for-processes

Provides: Carry tui.external_editor through typed configuration, bootstrap and reloaded local preferences to editor launch; parse quoted Linux command arguments and use VISUAL then EDITOR only when no command is configured, with explicit errors for empty or malformed commands.

Boundary: Protected harness buffer placement, write-policy checks and cleanup remain with normalize-base-roots-for-processes; terminal handoff, composer preservation and process failure reporting stay native, with no fallback after an invalid configured command and no user-config mutation.

Verification: Core configuration and generated-schema tests verify the option; focused TUI resolver and editor process tests verify precedence, quoted arguments, missing and invalid values, protected buffers, content return and cleanup.


